                <pb facs="0758" n="626" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg626"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/7623: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-09-11T12:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 11,
                                1926—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received September 11—7:55
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>388. My 386, September 10, noon. Commander in chief has instructed commander of
                    South China [<hi rendition="#italic">Yangtze?</hi>] Patrol to give necessary
                    protection and assistance to British subjects at Chungking in the absence of
                    British business interests [<hi rendition="#italic">naval vessel?</hi>]
                    there.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
